    <solution><alert>(a)</alert>
<m>z=2+x^2+y^2</m> is
an upward opening parabaloid with positive z intercept, centered on the z-axis, and so is
3.



<alert>(b)</alert>
<m>z=2(x^2 + y^2)</m> is
an upward opening parabaloid with zero z intercept, centered on the z-axis, and so is
none of these graphs.



<alert>(c)</alert>
<m>z=2-x+2y</m> is
a plane with positive x and z intercepts, and negative y intercept, and so is
none of these graphs.



<alert>(d)</alert>
<m>z=-2(x^2 + y^2)</m> is
a downward opening parabaloid with zero z intercept, centered on the z-axis, and so is
2.



<alert>(e)</alert>
<m>z=-2</m> is
a plane parallel to the x- and y-axes, with negative z intercept., and so is
1.



<alert>(f)</alert>
<m>z=2-x</m> is
a plane parallel to the y-axis, with positive x and z intercepts., and so is
4.



</solution>
